      "description": "Actual catalogue loading/failure pattern; thumbnails in the workshop are runtime model renders.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-block\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><span class=\"ds-image-slot\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Preview unavailable</span><span class=\"ds-caption\">Courtyard house</span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-block{font:14px/1.5 var(--font-body,'Segoe UI',sans-serif);color:var(--color-foreground,#28362d);min-height:44px;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--color-border,#7d8879);border-radius:var(--radius-sm,4px);background:var(--color-input,#fffdf7);cursor:pointer;transition:background var(--duration-fast,120ms) ease-out;width:88px;min-width:0;text-align:left;padding:4px;background:var(--color-surface-raised,#fffdf7)}.ds-image-slot{display:block;height:72px;background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}.ds-caption{display:block;font-size:12px;line-height:1.3;padding:4px;min-height:40px}.ds-block[aria-pressed=true]{outline:2px solid var(--color-primary,#355c3d);outline-offset:0;background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}.ds-block:active{background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}.ds-block:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-ring,#38633e);outline-offset:2px;}@media(hover:hover){.ds-block:hover{background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-block{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Preview label",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "preview-label",
      "description": "Informational label distinguishes the local preview from live Earth; it is not a toggle.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-preview\">Preview · not live Earth</span>",
      "css": ".ds-preview{font:12px/1.5 var(--font-body,'Segoe UI',sans-serif);color:var(--color-foreground,#28362d);background:var(--color-surface,#faf8f2);padding:4px 8px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm,4px)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Scene toolbar",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "scene-toolbar",
      "description": "Wrapped camera/history actions; disabled history and pressed sample toggle remain explicit.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-toolbar\" aria-label=\"Draft and camera controls\"><button disabled>Undo</button><button disabled>Redo</button><span class=\"ds-separator\"></span><button>Zoom in</button><button>Zoom out</button><button>Reset view</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Tile grid</button><button aria-pressed=\"true\">Sample people</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-toolbar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;padding:4px;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;background:var(--color-surface,#faf8f2);border-radius:var(--radius-md,8px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-raised,0 4px 16px rgb(40 54 45 / 12%))}.ds-toolbar button{font:14px/1.5 var(--font-body,'Segoe UI',sans-serif);color:var(--color-foreground,#28362d);min-height:44px;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--color-border,#7d8879);border-radius:var(--radius-sm,4px);background:var(--color-input,#fffdf7);cursor:pointer;transition:background var(--duration-fast,120ms) ease-out;font-size:12px;border:0;background:transparent}.ds-toolbar button[aria-pressed=true],.ds-toolbar button:active{background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}.ds-toolbar button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-ring,#38633e);outline-offset:2px;}.ds-toolbar button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}.ds-separator{width:1px;margin:8px 4px;background:var(--color-border,#7d8879)}@media(hover:hover){.ds-toolbar button:not(:disabled):hover{background:var(--color-muted,#e6e9dd)}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-toolbar button{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A neighborhood made from inspectable, reusable blocks",
    "overview": "This system records the neighborhood workshop at `/workshop.html` and `src/workshop/`, plus the shared 3D neighborhood appearance approved for live Earth on 11 October 2026. Scene art is shared through `src/world3d/neighborhood.ts`; the workshop interface tokens, typography, and component examples apply to the workshop only. The incumbent live HUD retains the authority of its existing `src/style.css` and components.\n\nEarthfolk materials give both neighborhoods their identity: cream buildings, timber, warm roofs, sage terrain, paths, and gardens. The workshop interface supports that world with quiet cream surfaces, dark green controls, compact native fields, and a generous angled 3D work surface. Segoe UI is the approved Operate workhorse face for this editor. Live Earth opens from a higher angled perspective, with softer ambient light and the shared sage background in overhead mode; its Orbit and Explore controls remain available.\n\nThe workshop world is a local planning document. Labels keep the draft distinct from live Earth, and sample people are explicitly presented as samples. Kernel identity, permissions, and publication authority remain outside this editor; its external-agent instructions do not invoke a central LLM or grant live authority. Shared appearance changes clone model materials while retaining source geometry, canonical footprints, and citizen identities.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A model-led neighborhood rather than decorative imagery.",
      "Cream interface surfaces and restrained dark green actions.",
      "Native controls, readable labels, and visible selection.",
      "A fixed angled workshop camera; a higher angled live default with Orbit and Explore retained.",
      "Explicit local-draft and sample-data language."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Material Scope Rule",
        "body": "Shared ART colors and material treatment apply to workshop and live neighborhood scenes; workshop controls retain their dark green palette, and live HUD styling retains its existing authority.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Controls Rule",
        "body": "Reserve raised interface depth for the scene toolbar; use borders, spacing, and selected-state marks for ordinary controls and groups.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep model identity, canonical footprints, and actual neighborhood geometry central to both scenes.",
      "Do use workshop CSS tokens for workshop controls and shared ART tokens for approved neighborhood scene materials.",
      "Do keep selected and invalid states legible through both text or semantics and color.",
      "Do label local drafts, sample people, and external-agent instructions accurately.",
      "Do keep keyboard fields and the draft-object list available alongside canvas interaction.",
      "Do preserve source provenance: Kenney CC0 licenses are recorded in `assets/kenney/LICENSE.md` and `public/models/NOTICE.md`; thumbnails are runtime renders of those existing assets."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't apply workshop HUD colors, typography, or component styling to live Earth without a separate approved interface change; the approved integration covers shared 3D appearance and touched accessibility controls.",
      "Don't imply local saving, plan import, or procedural generation publishes to shared Earth or grants Kernel permissions.",
      "Don't present sample people as live citizens or invoke a central LLM through workshop copy.",
      "Don't add a dark theme or shipping raster identity to a surface that currently has neither.",
      "Don't promise undo history survives reload; only the current draft is persisted."
    ]
  }
